---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../data/site.js';
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', name: 'About Vidatu', url: 'https://vidatu.com/about/' }];
---
<Base title="About Vidatu: how the films are made | Vidatu" description="Vidatu makes 30-second films about one true, surprising thing. Every character is built and animated in code, and every fact is sourced. Created and produced by SellnShip Solutions." path="/about/" ld={ld}>
<div class="wrap plain" style="padding-top:30px">
  <p class="crumbs"><a href={u('/')}>Vidatu</a> / About</p>
  <h1>Hidden rules, made visible.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Vidatu makes 30-second films about one true, surprising thing at a time. An alien audits human habits. A progress bar gets one life per fact. A hydrogen atom remembers the early universe.</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Made in code</h2>
    <p>Nothing here is filmed, and no AI video generator is used. Each character is a small program: shapes, materials, lights and a list of timed lines. A computer draws the film one frame at a time. Because the characters are programs, the same ones run live on this site, where you can move them and tap them.</p>
    <h2>The voices</h2>
    <p>The character voices are AI-generated and are labelled that way on every film. The Lab films have no voice at all: captions, and sound that is also made in code.</p>
    <h2>The facts</h2>
    <p>Every number in a film has a named source, listed on the film's page and on the <a href={u('/sources/')}>sources page</a>. Scripts are researched and written by the SellnShip team with the help of AI tools, every claim is checked against its source, and nothing is released until a person has watched and listened to it.</p>
    <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
    <p><b>Vidatu is created and produced by SellnShip Solutions Pvt. Ltd., Chandigarh, India.</b> The idea, the seven characters, the scripts, the fact-checking and the code that draws every frame are SellnShip's work. The same team makes films like these <a href={u('/brands/')}>for brands</a>.</p>
    <h2>Say hello</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:hello@vidatu.com">hello@vidatu.com</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@vidatutv">YouTube</a></p>
  </div>
  <div style="height:60px"></div>
</div>
</Base>
